# Template for the production server's env file (never commit the real one). It is the Jenkins
# credential help-prod-env (Secret file); scripts/deploy.sh uploads it as /opt/spolu/prod/.env,
# next to docker-compose.yml (docs/runbooks/deploy.md, "Jenkins").
#
# MUST be copied from the current server's /opt/spolu/test/.env when the data moves there
# (they are not new secrets; new values would break existing data):
#   APP_SECRET           signs sessions and tokens: a new one logs everyone out, disconnects the
#                        Claude (MCP) connectors and breaks links already sent (unsubscribe,
#                        calendar feeds, Teams links)
#   VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY, VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY, VAPID_SUBJECT
#                        Web Push: new keys silently drop every existing push subscription
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD    only if the pgdata volume itself is copied; with a dump and restore
#                        (scripts/move-data.sh, docs/runbooks/server-move.md) a new password is fine
#   and every integration key the old server has: SMTP_* / ELASTIC_EMAIL_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY,
#   TEAMS_*, TICKETS_API_KEY, EGRANT_* (eGrant calls these webhooks with the same keys).
#
# Proxy mode (behind the company's Apache, ADR 0068): BEHIND_PROXY, HTTP_PORT, DOMAIN,
# PUBLIC_URL and REDIRECT_DOMAINS come from the Jenkins job variables; deploy.sh writes them (and
# COMPOSE_FILE) into the server's .env and drops any lines with these keys from this file.
# Only TRUSTED_PROXIES (below) belongs here, and only when the defaults do not fit.

# Image repository and tag to run; deploy.sh overwrites both with the deployed image and git SHA
IMAGE=registry.example.com/egrant/spolu
TAG=latest
# Public domain (Apache serves it in proxy mode). scripts/deploy.sh overrides DOMAIN,
# PUBLIC_URL and REDIRECT_DOMAINS (old domains redirected here) from its own variables.
DOMAIN=help.example.com
# PostgreSQL password, URL-safe, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`; compose builds DATABASE_URL from it, so DATABASE_URL is not set here.
# It only applies when the pgdata volume is first created. To change it later run ALTER USER spolu PASSWORD '...' first, then update this file.
# The app refuses to start with change-me or spolu.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
# Optional: backup time (HH:MM, avoid 02:00-02:59: skipped by the March DST change) and timezone for the backup container
#BACKUP_HOUR=03:30
#BACKUP_TZ=Europe/Bratislava

# Public base URL of the app, used in links and emails
PUBLIC_URL=https://help.example.com
# Email of the first superadmin account, created on first boot
SUPERADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# Display name of the superadmin; optional, defaults to the part of the email before @.
SUPERADMIN_NAME=
# Secret for signing sessions and tokens, at least 32 characters (openssl rand -hex 32).
# The app refuses to start with this placeholder.
APP_SECRET=change-me-to-a-random-string-of-32-chars-or-more
# Deployed environments send real email through Elastic Email, here over authenticated SMTP.
# Alternative: EMAIL_DRIVER=elastic with ELASTIC_EMAIL_API_KEY=<api key> (and no SMTP_* lines);
# BULK_EMAIL_DRIVER then defaults to elastic too (unset, it follows EMAIL_DRIVER).
EMAIL_DRIVER=smtp
SMTP_HOST=smtp.elasticemail.com
# 465 = implicit TLS (SMTP_SECURE defaults to true on 465, false otherwise)
SMTP_PORT=465
# Elastic Email SMTP login and password (set both or neither)
SMTP_USER=change-me
SMTP_PASSWORD=change-me
# Sender address for all outgoing email
MAIL_FROM=Help by eGrant <noreply@example.com>
# Bulk email (Phase 23). Before the first real send switch to the Elastic API (the marketing
# endpoint /v4/emails); until then bulk email goes over the SMTP settings above. The key needs
# the SendHttp, ViewSuppressions and ModifySuppressions access levels.
# BULK_EMAIL_DRIVER=elastic
# ELASTIC_EMAIL_API_KEY=change-me
# Sender of bulk email on a domain verified in Elastic; optional, defaults to MAIL_FROM
# MAIL_FROM_BULK=eGrant <info@example.com>
# Upper bound of bulk emails a minute (default 120)
# BULK_EMAIL_PER_MINUTE=120
# elastic (default: the footer link passes through Elastic's unsubscribe wrapper) | spolu (only
# after Elastic's support removed its forced link and the List-Unsubscribe header setting is off)
# BULK_EMAIL_UNSUBSCRIBE=elastic
# Opens, clicks, bounces and complaints (ADR 0070, docs/integrations/elastic-email.md): the
# signing secret of Elastic's webhook to https://<domain>/api/bulk-email/webhook (POST JSON,
# signed). Set = open and click tracking on. Needs BULK_EMAIL_DRIVER=elastic.
# ELASTIC_WEBHOOK_SECRET=change-me
# Web Push (VAPID): set all three or none (none = push off). Generate the keys once per
# environment with `pnpm --filter @spolu/server vapid:generate`; never change them afterwards.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=change-me
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=change-me
# mailto: or https: contact for the push services
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:admin@example.com
# Milliseconds a group's email notifications wait so several events go out as one (default 600000)
# EMAIL_BATCH_DELAY_MS=600000
# Login code requests allowed per minute and IP; an office behind one IP shares it (default 10)
# LOGIN_CODES_PER_MINUTE=10
# Invite-link email submissions per minute and IP (default 10)
# JOIN_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=10
# AI task split ("Turn into tasks" on a chat message). Optional: without a key the action is hidden.
# Never set AI_PROVIDER=fake on a server (it is a canned splitter for dev and e2e); in production the
# app refuses to start with it unless AI_ALLOW_FAKE=1, which only the e2e web server sets.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional, default gpt-5-mini (also the meeting summaries)
#OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
# Optional: the chat composer's AI text tools (Phase 28), default gpt-5.4-mini with low reasoning
#OPENAI_TEXT_MODEL=gpt-5.4-mini
#OPENAI_TEXT_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# Meeting transcription (Phase 30) and chat voice input (Phase 28): the OpenAI key above covers it (default model gpt-transcribe).
# To switch to ElevenLabs Scribe, set both lines below.
#OPENAI_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=gpt-transcribe
#TRANSCRIPTION_PROVIDER=elevenlabs
#ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Microsoft Teams (T1, docs/integrations/teams.md). Optional: unset = Teams is off and hidden.
# Tenant and client ids from the Entra app, then a client secret OR a certificate (key file
# inside the container, see the commented volume in docker-compose.yml, and its thumbprint).
#TEAMS_TENANT_ID=
#TEAMS_CLIENT_ID=
#TEAMS_CLIENT_SECRET=
#TEAMS_CERT_PATH=/run/secrets/spolu/teams.pem
#TEAMS_CERT_THUMBPRINT=
# eGrant webhooks (docs/integrations/egrant.md). Optional: empty = off or fallback, as noted.
# Bearer keys are at least 16 characters, signing secrets at least 32 (openssl rand -hex 32);
# none is ever logged.
# Ticket intake key (POST /api/tickets/intake); empty = 503 intake_disabled. scripts/deploy.sh
# overrides it from its own TICKETS_API_KEY when that is set.
TICKETS_API_KEY=
# Groups webhook key (PUT /api/egrant/groups). Strongly recommended: empty = TICKETS_API_KEY
# opens it too, and that key can then create and deactivate any client group.
EGRANT_GROUPS_API_KEY=
# Managers and projects webhook keys; empty = they use TICKETS_API_KEY.
EGRANT_MANAGERS_API_KEY=
EGRANT_PROJECTS_API_KEY=
# HMAC request signing per webhook (ADR 0042); set = calls must carry X-Spolu-Timestamp and
# X-Spolu-Signature, else 401. Empty = not signed.
EGRANT_TICKETS_SIGNING_SECRET=
EGRANT_MANAGERS_SIGNING_SECRET=
EGRANT_GROUPS_SIGNING_SECRET=
EGRANT_PROJECTS_SIGNING_SECRET=
# NODE_ENV, PORT, WEB_DIST_DIR, FILES_DIR and APP_VERSION are set by the image; DATABASE_URL by compose.
# Proxy mode only: addresses whose X-Forwarded-For/-Proto Caddy believes (deploy/Caddyfile.proxy).
# Default 127.0.0.1/8 ::1 172.16.0.0/12: loopback and Docker's default bridge networks, which is
# where Apache's connections to 127.0.0.1:HTTP_PORT arrive from. Narrow it to the compose
# network's gateway (docker network inspect spolu_default) when the office LAN uses 172.16.0.0/12.
#TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1/8 ::1 172.16.0.0/12
